"""OpenTruck - VIN engine-code tables for light-duty (OBD-II) vehicles.

Resolves the engine (displacement, cylinders, configuration, fuel) fully
OFFLINE from the VIN: the WMI (positions 1-3) selects the manufacturer's
VIN layout, position 8 is the engine code, and where a code is shared
across vehicle lines (e.g. 1FT "R" = 5.4 F-150 vs 6.4 Super Duty) the
table keys on VIN positions 4-7 (and 10-17 where the manufacturer uses
them) so the exact VIN context resolves the engine. This replaces the
former online NHTSA vPIC lookup (removed for full-offline identification).

Source: compiled from the NHTSA vPIC standalone database
(vPICList_lite_2026_10, plain-SQL edition, downloaded 2026-11-15) - the
same public dataset the vPIC web API decodes from. Entries are included
only where the dataset is unambiguous for that WMI + engine code + model
year + VIN context; a code whose data still conflicts is not guessed.
Sampled entries were verified against the live DecodeVinValues API
(2026-11-15). US-market vehicles only; model years 1996-2027 (the OBD-II
era this table serves).

Lookup: engine_for_vin(vin) -> description string, or None when unknown.

DISCLAIMER: The data in this file is a compilation assembled from sources
found through ordinary internet search (standards documents, public service
documentation and similar material). It is not an official publication of
SAE International, ISO, NHTSA or any vehicle, engine or component
manufacturer, and the OpenTruck project has no affiliation with, sponsorship
from, or endorsement by any of them; all brand names are the property of
their respective owners. The contents may be inaccurate, incomplete or out of
date and are provided as-is, without warranty of any kind.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

from typing import Optional

from lookup.vin import model_year

# wmi -> engine code ("?" = any position-8 char for single-engine layouts)
#   -> [(year_from, year_to, ctx_4_to_7, ctx_10_to_17, facts), ...]
# ctx tuples: "" = any char at that VIN position, otherwise the allowed
#   characters (no separators). ctx_4_to_7 indexes VIN positions 4,5,6,7;
#   ctx_10_to_17 positions 10..17 (ANY4/ANY8 are the all-any tuples).
# facts (_Fn pool below) = (displacement L, cylinders, configuration
# V/I/W/U, fuel code, turbo, engine model) with None for fields the
# dataset did not carry.
ANY4 = ("", "", "", "")
ANY8 = ("", "", "", "", "", "", "", "")

